messages[14]{user,text}:
  user_1,"Hey, uh, is this Vikram? ... [00:00]"
  user_2,"Yes, speaking. Hi Reyansh, how can I help you today?"
  user_1,"I was just checking on my health policy... I think it might be... expired? ... [00:15]"
  user_2,"Let me pull that up. One sec... [typing]"
  user_2,"Okay, I see policy #HC-2023-9876. It actually shows an expiration date of 15/09/2026. So yeah, it's just passed."
  user_1,"Ah, okay. So... what does that mean for me? Can I still use it?"
  user_2,"Once a health policy expires, you can't file new claims. You can renew, though—there's a renewal window up to 30 days after expiry."
  user_1,"Umm, I didn't get any renewal notice. [sighs] I guess I missed it."
  user_2,"No worries, we can still process a renewal. It'll just be a new term starting 01/10/2026, with a small lapse fee."
  user_1,"Got it. What are the premiums now? I think they went up."
  user_2,"The new annual premium is $1,250, up from $1,100 last year, due to the updated medical cost index."
  user_1,"Alright... I need to think about it. Can you send me the renewal quote via email?"
  user_2,"Sure thing, I'll email you the quote right after we hang up. Anything else?"
  user_1,"No, that's all. Thanks, Vikram."